            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "Gvrhu",
              "name": "Rule Note",
              "fill": "#645A5A",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Preview approximation: outline words render with a soft-gray fill instead of literal .vp-outline hollow text — Pencil cannot render text stroke (the live site uses -webkit-text-stroke on transparent fill; there is no direct Pencil equivalent). The soft-gray fill communicates the visual weight demotion; on live, this becomes an actual glyph outline.\n\nRule TBD — options on the table: (a) first line always solid + rest outline, (b) semantic (brand/product name solid + descriptor outline), (c) fully freeform per heading. Confirm which the CMS field/logic actually implements before locking. ZH sample confirms the pattern applies to CJK glyphs — the earlier knockout bug is fixed on live.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "Mona Sans",
              "fontSize": 12,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
